# Implementation Plan - Phase 4 – UI/UX Design

Implement Phase 4 (UI/UX Design) of the Leitner Learning Platform by establishing a comprehensive UI Design Document and building an interactive, high-fidelity web prototype. The prototype will simulate the entire user flow, allowing the client to experience the look, feel, and navigation of the system.

To provide maximum value, the interactive prototype will feature a **"Wireframe Mode" vs. "High-Fidelity Mode" toggle**. This allows the reviewer to inspect either the raw wireframe structure or the final, styled, premium user interface with rich aesthetics, gradients, and micro-animations.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The interactive web prototype is written in Vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. This makes it self-contained, requiring no external compilation tools (like NPM or Vite) to run, ensuring it can be opened instantly in any browser.

